// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg1200_docks.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~If you have any heavy luggage packing onto the next ship, talk to the Harbor Master. Once I have your name on the list, I will help you put your baggage on the ship.~
@2 = ~Contrary to what you may think, us, kobolds are not some brainless fools. How many times did I have a human come up to me and ask how is it possible some of us speak common with such exemplary academic professionalism. I am a classy kobold. I love literature, I know how to read and I aspire to be a bard. Why can't people understand that your alignment and path you go down is rooted in your environment, not your heritage. I am a proud Baldurian.~
@3 = ~Talk to Harbor Master if you want to charter a ship. He is inside this massive building behind me. Take care.~
@4 = ~If you have any inquiries about hiring a ship speak to Harbor Master.~
@5 = ~Nothing like the smell of the sea. I really despise swimming or ships in general, but the fresh scent of seawater filling my nostrils is an unforgettable feeling. This is what I live for.~
@6 = ~That old fool, Ragefast is no better than Ramazith. The two seem to be having some sort of personal issue with each other. I really hope they settle things with each other and stop making a fuss that whole city is forced to hear about.~
@7 = ~Keep away from Iron Throne building. Wrong things are happening in there. A Flaming Fist member was murdered there not long ago. Someone threw him down from the rooftop. And that isn't all. My neighbour is working inside as a bureaucrat and what she told me as of late shook me to the core. She claims one of the other workers became cold, distant and standoffish lately. She pressed him about it and she swore that his eyes changed colour for a split second.~
@8 = ~This place reeks of fish. I should've taken that into consideration when I picked a house close to the docks.~
@9 = ~Some wandering bard sang about a mind flayer base somewhere underneath our feet. Sounds ominous, but it's just a tale. Right?~
@10 = ~Adventurers, huh? If you have enough experience and courage, clean out the Durlag's tower south from here. It is said to contain a huge amount of treasure secured by traps and the undead. I bet somebody already cleansed the place from all evil dwellers but... you might find a gem or two.~
@11 = ~Keep away from the edge, please. Last week I had to save two silly teenage women who fell down to the water because they disregarded my warnings. Silly, silly people.~
@12 = ~Have a nice day.~
@13 = ~Call me a bigot, but I am against kobolds cluttering up our lovely city. In fact, whenever I hear my daughter asking me if she can hug a kobold cause they look cuddly, my blood is boiling in my veins. Maybe I am biased due to what happened at Nashkel mines but I just do not trust them.~
@14 = ~I wouldn't approach Umberlee's temple without a good reason. Their goddess is called a bitch queen for a reason. The word applies to her priestesses too.~
@15 = ~Me like this place. Me grow up in wilds but friend say this a great city. Me have friends, and me have cat. Happy to call this place home.~
@16 = ~What are you looking at!~
@17 = ~I didn't expect someone like… you in this city.~
@18 = ~Does Flaming Fist know you're here?~
@19 = ~You hideous creature. Draw steel!~
@20 = ~I'll leave you alone.~
@21 = ~What I do here is my own business. Now, walk away and mind your business.~
@22 = ~For your information, they do. I may not be welcome here but I have no quarrel with you. I am here to trade, that's it. Now, can you leave me?~
@23 = ~Your last words ever spoken.~
@24 = ~As you should.~
@25 = ~B-be careful, my friend. I believe it to b-be a Gith-Githyanki. Dangerous creatures operating on ingrained sense of r-racial supremacy who likely view as as lesser and expendable.~
@26 = ~Boo does not like the look of that creature. Had we not been in populated area, it'd be best to deal with this thing. He is up to no good for sure.~
@27 = ~Baldurians laws appear to be incomplete if they let just about anyone to walk in through the gates. What were they thinking allowing a Githyanki to a civilised location such as this.~
@28 = ~Had I been the guard I would not condone permissions to let a hideous beast like this to the city, alas we live in times where visibly everyone does what they want to. Let us turn around and leave before it decides to sharpen it's sword against our bones.~
@29 = ~Did you know they used to have a beholder's head hanging in the Elfsong Tavern? Decorated the wall above the fireplace quite nicely, it did. Alyth only took it down because some drunk complained. Imagine removing a fine decoration just because an intoxicated fellow wouldn't stop whining. Pah!~
@30 = ~The Iron Throne is not a recreation area. Unless you have pressing business inside, please turn back.~
